framework for building building  client applications in HTML,CSS,JS/Typescript

Benefits:
-> gives our applications a clean structure
-> includes a lot of reusable code
-> makes applns more testable
-> hot reload - reloaded the page automatically
Architecture:
frontend (html,css,ang,js) <---HTTP---> backend(Data+APIs, businesslogic)
API(application programming interface) :
    endpoints that are accessible vis HTTP protocol

Angular Application:
Components :
    -> what user can see and interact with, data binding happeniing between input fields
    -> we can have multiple Components
Services:
    -> handles data
    -> communicate with rest apis to load our data via db
    -> spread the loaded data onfo to all our Components
Modules:
    -> encapsulation and structure

SPA(Single page application):
- Dwonload the application initially
- update only what got changed
- recues loading times and server load
-> runs on a webserver -> requires node.js and npm

stackblitzz

Angular CLI:
- this is a node package
"npm install -g @angular/cli" -> -g for global installation
"ng --version / ng v"

creating angular project:
"ng new hello-world"
"ng serve -o"(opens the browser)

angular.json:
    - specify different configurations
    - ex: prd env, local env, test env

src :
  - index.html: root fo  the appln
  - <app-root></app-root> custom tag

-------------------------------------------------------
COMPONENTS:
- main building block of your application
app.ts:
- @Component turns the class to the component
@Component({
  selector: 'app-root', #html selector used to render this component
  templateUrl: './app.component.html', #component connected to this html (both ways)
  styleUrls: ['./app.component.css']
})
export class AppComponent { #export it so that we can import it in other modules#
  title = 'appointment-app';
  message = 'hello world'
}

generate a component:
    - "ng g component appointment-list"
Rendering component:
- use the component selector in main html/component

One-way Binding:
    - display the content to show on the template(html)
    - we use {{}}
    - template:
        {{message}}

app.module.ts:
    - decripcated in latest versions
    - main configuration file in older Angular apps (NgModule-based architecture).

Interface:
    - "ng generate interface models/appointment"
    - creates model folder with interface

Adding functionaliy:
Two-way data binding:
html->component save value from iput we got in html to component
- we need forms module for two way data binding
in app.module.ts:
- import { FormsModule } from '@angular/forms';
- and then add it to imports so that components can use it
    imports: [
        BrowserModule,
        FormsModule
    ],
- inside forms module we have "ngmodel" which we need for two way data binding
- in html 
    <input [(ngModel)]="newAppointmentTitle" placeholder="Appointement description">
    <input [(ngModel)]="newAppointmentDate" type="date" placeholder="Appointement date">
here newAppointmentTitle,newAppointmentDate from component are upadted to reflect the value the user has entered.

looping functionality:
ngFor:
    - for looping in Aungulat temple we use directive called ngFor
    <li *ngFor="let appointment of appointments">
        {{appointment.id}}
        {{appointment.title}}
        {{appointment.date | date:'dd.MM.yyyy'}} <!-- pipe the date to the format dd.MM.yyyy-->
    </li>
    - ngFor gets notified from the nagular change detection eveytime a new appointment is added and with reloading adds the new item.

delete functionality:
    <li *ngFor="let appointment of appointments; index as i">
        {{appointment.title}}{{appointment.date | date:'dd.MM.yyyy'}}
        <button (click)="deleteAppointment(i)">Delete</button>
    </li>

storing data:
- we can use dbs, currently for learning purpose using browser storage
Localstorage:
    - convert from typscript to json
    /*key -> appointments, value->json data*/
    - localStorage.setItem("appointments",JSON.stringify(this.appointments))

ngOnInit:
- load data when we reload the appn
- when the component gets initiallized that is when we want to load data
(all appointments stored laod when appointement component gets initialised, ie when appns starts or reloaded)
LifeCycleHooks:
    ngOnInit()
    - import { OnInit } from '@angular/core';
    - export class AppointmentListComponent implements OnInit{}
    - we have to implement this lifecycle hook method otherwise error will be thrown
        ngOnInit(): void {
                throw new Error('Method not implemented.');
            }

BOOTSTRAP:
"npm install bootstrap"
styles.css:
    @import "~bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css"